{"claim_id": "R1-01", "task_id": "R1-hygiene", "claim": "The .gitignore covering the 6.5 GB lean/.lake/ tree sits INSIDE the session folder, at sessions/2026-09-17/CT-S1-THEOREM/lean/.gitignore, not at the repo root. git status --porcelain --untracked-files=all reports exactly one .gitignore path, that one, as untracked; git diff on the repo-root .gitignore is empty. No unintended repo change.", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "git status / git diff", "output_hash": "89ac0be68608adf4d20c86450f7c8a024b34a079b94148d0aecb3f52978aa17d", "label": "INSPECTED", "label_before_r2": "STRUCTURAL", "audit_r2": "Relabelled INSPECTED under operator ruling 1(a): established by direct inspection of named files at commit 08aa0e2381b3dc37ee54a3200b7272755ca11d59; valid only for that commit.", "amended_in": "CT-R1-AUDIT/R2"}
{"claim_id": "R1-02", "task_id": "R1-proof-audit", "claim": "AUDIT FINDING, now repaired. theorem.tex Theorem thm:radius Step 3 asserted without proof that the balanced multinomial coefficient (dn)!/(n!)^d is the largest over compositions of dn into d parts. The assertion is LOAD-BEARING: the lower bound d^{dn}/(dn+1)^{d-1} is obtained as max >= average and fails without maximality. A complete proof was added by the exchange argument: if k_i >= k_j+2, moving one unit from part i to part j multiplies the coefficient by k_i/(k_j+1) >= (k_j+2)/(k_j+1) > 1, so any maximiser over the finite set of compositions has |k_i-k_j| <= 1, which with sum k_i = dn forces all k_i = n. Steps 1,2,4,5 were checked and are correct as written; no Stirling or Gamma asymptotics appears anywhere in part (i), as the prompt required.", "evidence_type": "proof", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "theorem.tex (thm:radius, Step 3 sub-lemma)", "output_hash": "89ac0be68608adf4d20c86450f7c8a024b34a079b94148d0aecb3f52978aa17d", "label": "PROVEN", "audit_r2": "Retagged evidence_type file_inspection -> proof under operator ruling 1: this is a mathematical claim whose proof happens to live in a file, not a claim about repository contents. Label unchanged.", "amended_in": "CT-R1-AUDIT/R2", "review": "self", "audit_r3": "Operator review #3 ruling 1: evidence_type 'proof' accepted, with a mandatory `review` field. 'self' = checked only by the agent that wrote it; 'cold' = read by an independent session without its derivation history; 'lean' = machine-checked with no sorry on the claim's path. PROVEN may stand on a 'self' claim, but anything entering a deposit requires 'cold' or 'lean'.", "review_note": "self: checked only by the session that produced it. For a computation this means no independent reimplementation; re-running the original script would not change this."}
{"claim_id": "R1-03", "task_id": "R1-gap-G1", "claim": "Gap G1 closed. With h(n) := Gamma(n+1-r) n^r / Gamma(n+1), the identity Gamma(x+1)=x Gamma(x) alone gives h(n)/h(n-1) = (1 - r/n)(1 - 1/n)^(-r) = 1 + O(1/n^2); since sum O(1/n^2) converges, the telescoping product converges to a finite nonzero h_inf, and the tail of a convergent sum O(1/m^2) is O(1/n), so h(n) = h_inf (1 + O(1/n)). The entire O(1/n) error bookkeeping is therefore self-contained. The sole imported ingredient is the constant h_inf = 1, cited to DLMF (5.11.12), Sec 5.11(iii) 'Ratios', where G_0(a,b) = 1, with a = 1-r, b = 1, z = n. The equation number and statement were verified against dlmf.nist.gov/5.11 directly, not from memory. Claim S1-04 is upgraded STRUCTURAL -> PROVEN modulo that named citation.", "evidence_type": "proof", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "theorem.tex (thm:growth, Step 3)", "output_hash": "89ac0be68608adf4d20c86450f7c8a024b34a079b94148d0aecb3f52978aa17d", "label": "PROVEN", "audit_r2": "Retagged evidence_type file_inspection -> proof under operator ruling 1: this is a mathematical claim whose proof happens to live in a file, not a claim about repository contents. Label unchanged.", "amended_in": "CT-R1-AUDIT/R2", "review": "self", "audit_r3": "Operator review #3 ruling 1: evidence_type 'proof' accepted, with a mandatory `review` field. 'self' = checked only by the agent that wrote it; 'cold' = read by an independent session without its derivation history; 'lean' = machine-checked with no sorry on the claim's path. PROVEN may stand on a 'self' claim, but anything entering a deposit requires 'cold' or 'lean'.", "review_note": "self: checked only by the session that produced it. For a computation this means no independent reimplementation; re-running the original script would not change this."}
{"claim_id": "R1-04", "task_id": "R1-labels", "claim": "Label amendments applied by apply_audit.py across five claims.jsonl files, 13 claims amended. Downgraded PROVEN -> STRUCTURAL: S2-05 (a negative grep result cannot prove absence), S3A-03 and S3A-06 (file_inspection, and partly negative results). Upgraded STRUCTURAL -> PROVEN: S1-04 (Gap G1 closed). Upheld with basis restated: S1-01, S1-02, S1-03, S3B-01, S3B-03, S4-03, S4-04, S4-05, S4-06, S4-07. Each amended row carries audit_r1, amended_in, and where the label moved, label_before. Corpus after R1: 47 claims, 16 PROVEN, 21 STRUCTURAL, 10 VERIFIED; every row parses and carries exactly one label.", "evidence_type": "computation", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "apply_audit.py", "output_hash": "2b0ee9bcc5e24cba84c050e12d263dc7861211a02a319bcadde96db62fdaaa7b", "label": "STRUCTURAL", "amended_in": "CT-R1-AUDIT/R2"}
{"claim_id": "R1-05", "task_id": "R1-companion-version", "claim": "SUPERSEDED BY DIRECT EVIDENCE (round R2), and the conclusion is reversed. R1 concluded that the companion was absent from the repo so Conjecture 4.1 could be neither confirmed nor refuted. The paper has now been downloaded from Zenodo and all three versions are in sessions/2026-09-17/CT-R1-AUDIT/refs/: v1.0 (20455090, sha256 c07c97d6..., 10 pp), v1.1 (20480603, sha256 e07c1dda..., 12 pp), v1.2 (20481592, sha256 a5d9e264..., 12 pp). Conjecture 4.1 EXISTS in v1.2; the object numbered 4.1 is a Theorem in v1.0 and v1.1. The operator's version hypothesis is CONFIRMED. The repo's bibitem{Vquad} cites v1.0, which is why the label was not found by anyone reading only the cited version. Note also that the companion's published title differs from the title in the repo's bibliography entry.", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "repo-wide title-string search", "output_hash": "89ac0be68608adf4d20c86450f7c8a024b34a079b94148d0aecb3f52978aa17d", "label": "INSPECTED", "label_before_r2": "STRUCTURAL", "audit_r2": "Relabelled INSPECTED under operator ruling 1(a): established by direct inspection of named files at commit 08aa0e2381b3dc37ee54a3200b7272755ca11d59; valid only for that commit.", "claim_before_r2": "The 'Conjecture 4.1 does not exist' finding is RETRACTED as a citation defect and restated as missing data. What CT-S4 searched was sessions/2026-06-15/VQUAD-PERIODREP-PAPER-001, the PERIOD-REP paper, not the V_quad companion. The companion is a distinct document, cited as bibitem{Vquad} in sections/section-9-references.md L6-11 ('The V_quad polynomial continued fraction: a Painleve-V standalone closure on the Sakai surface D5^(1)', Zenodo, version DOI 10.5281/zenodo.20455090, concept 10.5281/zenodo.20455089). A repo-wide search for its title string returns ONLY citing occurrences: bibliography entries, LaTeX preambles, and outline mentions. No copy of the companion exists in this repo at ANY version, so Conjecture 4.1 can be neither confirmed nor refuted here. The operator's v1.0/v1.1 hypothesis is likewise NOT confirmed: there is no copy to inspect. The only companion version number visible anywhere is the v1.2 inside the bibitem{StokesNote} citation string, which is a citation, not a copy. Finding S4-F1 stands as a pure missing-data finding.", "amended_in": "CT-R1-AUDIT/R2"}
{"claim_id": "R1-06", "task_id": "R1-citation", "claim": "The operator-supplied classification citation is VERIFIED against the publisher and a copy is in the session folder. Marius van der Put and Masa-Hiko Saito, 'Moduli spaces for linear differential equations and the Painleve equations', Annales de l'Institut Fourier, Tome 59, no. 7 (2009), pp. 2611-2667, DOI 10.5802/aif.2502, open access via Centre Mersenne. File refs/vanderPut-Saito-AIF-2009-59-7-2611.pdf, 1058380 bytes, 58 pages, title page matching the stated volume/issue/pages. It is the correct source: the Introduction states the paper constructs the ten rank-two isomonodromic families and explicitly allows 'all possible irregular singularities including ramification', which Jimbo-Miwa-Ueno's tables exclude. Caveat for re-searchers: the PDF uses the fi ligature, so grep for 'ramified' returns zero hits; search 'rami'.", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "publisher metadata + PDF title page", "output_hash": "1666bd6be824a99fc0b48adbe48233a9b2a520fd7e8adf187e98d22525473605", "label": "INSPECTED", "label_before_r2": "STRUCTURAL", "audit_r2": "Relabelled INSPECTED under operator ruling 1(a): established by direct inspection of named files at commit 08aa0e2381b3dc37ee54a3200b7272755ca11d59; valid only for that commit.", "amended_in": "CT-R1-AUDIT/R2"}
{"claim_id": "R1-07", "task_id": "R1-table", "claim": "Table 2.1 'Classification of Families' (p. 2635) extracted verbatim into CLASSIFICATION-TABLE.md, together with the selection rule on p. 2634. The paper identifies the ten families by their Katz-invariant multiset, not by number. The D5-tilde / PV row is (r(0), r(1), r(infinity), r(t)) = (0, 0, 1, -) with dim P = 3: two regular singular points and one irregular point of Katz invariant 1, hence UNRAMIFIED. This confirms from a verified primary source the premise that P5 was given and that CT-S4 had to take on trust. P5 step 3's halt condition is lifted.", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "CLASSIFICATION-TABLE.md", "output_hash": "18d4d16eba0108373d899fab1095312c12cbae2466ce9973737b45cfa21417a7", "label": "INSPECTED", "label_before_r2": "STRUCTURAL", "audit_r2": "Relabelled INSPECTED under operator ruling 1(a): established by direct inspection of named files at commit 08aa0e2381b3dc37ee54a3200b7272755ca11d59; valid only for that commit.", "amended_in": "CT-R1-AUDIT/R2"}
{"claim_id": "R1-08", "task_id": "R1-table-match", "claim": "Matching CT-S4 and CT-S5B-COVER outputs against Table 2.1. System A (the f = Sum Q_n z^n ODE for b(n)=3n^2+n+1) has ramified Katz 1/2 at z=0, ramified Katz 1/2 at z=infinity, and no other singular point, so its Katz multiset is (1/2, -, 1/2), which is the D8-tilde row, PIII(D8). Its pullback along z=w^2 has unramified Katz 1 at w=0 and at infinity, multiset (1, -, 1), which is the D6-tilde row, PIII(D6). Both matches are exact and mutually consistent, since a quadratic cover is the classical relation between PIII(D8) and PIII(D6). NEITHER is D5-tilde / PV. Because the Katz multiset is an invariant of the family, no change of variable moves between rows.", "evidence_type": "proof", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "CLASSIFICATION-TABLE.md", "output_hash": "18d4d16eba0108373d899fab1095312c12cbae2466ce9973737b45cfa21417a7", "label": "STRUCTURAL", "audit_r2": "Retagged evidence_type file_inspection -> proof under operator ruling 1: this is a mathematical claim whose proof happens to live in a file, not a claim about repository contents. Label unchanged.", "amended_in": "CT-R1-AUDIT/R2", "review": "self", "audit_r3": "Operator review #3 ruling 1: evidence_type 'proof' accepted, with a mandatory `review` field. 'self' = checked only by the agent that wrote it; 'cold' = read by an independent session without its derivation history; 'lean' = machine-checked with no sorry on the claim's path. PROVEN may stand on a 'self' claim, but anything entering a deposit requires 'cold' or 'lean'.", "review_note": "self: checked only by the session that produced it. For a computation this means no independent reimplementation; re-running the original script would not change this."}
{"claim_id": "R1-09", "task_id": "R1-table-match", "claim": "System B (L_phi) taken at face value has one irregular Katz-1 point at z=0 plus THREE regular singular points (rho_pm = (-1 +- i sqrt 11)/2 and z=infinity), which is not a row of Table 2.1, since the table admits #S=4 only when all r(p)=0. If exactly one of those three is an APPARENT singularity, and so carries no moduli and is not counted, the effective multiset becomes (0, 0, 1), which is the D5-tilde / PV row. VQ-N1 records apparent indices [0,0]. Neither CT-S5B-COVER nor this session recomputed the apparency of rho_pm or of infinity, so the D5-tilde match for System B is not established.", "evidence_type": "proof", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "CLASSIFICATION-TABLE.md", "output_hash": "18d4d16eba0108373d899fab1095312c12cbae2466ce9973737b45cfa21417a7", "label": "CONJECTURED", "audit_r2": "Retagged evidence_type file_inspection -> proof under operator ruling 1: this is a mathematical claim whose proof happens to live in a file, not a claim about repository contents. Label unchanged.", "amended_in": "CT-R1-AUDIT/R2", "review": "self", "audit_r3": "Operator review #3 ruling 1: evidence_type 'proof' accepted, with a mandatory `review` field. 'self' = checked only by the agent that wrote it; 'cold' = read by an independent session without its derivation history; 'lean' = machine-checked with no sorry on the claim's path. PROVEN may stand on a 'self' claim, but anything entering a deposit requires 'cold' or 'lean'.", "review_note": "self: checked only by the session that produced it. For a computation this means no independent reimplementation; re-running the original script would not change this."}
{"claim_id": "R1-10", "task_id": "R1-p5b-review", "claim": "CT-S5B-COVER's two central computations were re-derived independently by hand and confirmed. The normal-form pullback rule R = (phi')^2 r(phi) - (1/2) Schwarzian(phi) follows from v'' - (phi''/phi') v' - (phi')^2 r(phi) v = 0 together with the standard reduction R = a^2/4 + a'/2 - b. For phi = w^2, Schwarzian = -3/(2w^2), giving correction +3/(4w^2), and R(w) = 4w^2 r_A(w^2) + 3/(4w^2) = (-48w^4 - 53w^2 + 48)/(36w^4); the numerator at w=0 is 48, nonzero, so the pole order is 4, even, hence unramified with Katz 1. At infinity the potential is (48t^4 - 80t^2 - 48)/(36t^4), numerator -48 at t=0, pole order 4, Katz 1. For phi = 1/x the Schwarzian vanishes and R(x) = r_B(1/x)/x^4 = (12x^4+4x^3+4x^2+11)/(4(3x^2+x+1)^2), with roots (-1 +- i sqrt 11)/6 and R(0) = 11/4 finite so x=0 is ordinary. Every value matches the agent's output exactly. Separately, S5B-C2 is labelled STRUCTURAL but is arguably PROVEN; the conservative label was left in place.", "evidence_type": "computation", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "hand re-derivation, recorded in AUDIT.md section 5", "output_hash": "89ac0be68608adf4d20c86450f7c8a024b34a079b94148d0aecb3f52978aa17d", "label": "PROVEN", "amended_in": "CT-R1-AUDIT/R2"}
{"claim_id": "R1-11", "task_id": "R1-build", "claim": "theorem.tex recompiles after the R1 repairs with pdflatex: a final pass reports NO undefined references and NO undefined citations, and writes theorem.pdf at 7 pages, 343115 bytes (previously 6 pages). A thebibliography block with the DLMF entry was added to resolve the new citation.", "evidence_type": "build", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "pdflatex theorem.tex", "output_hash": "89ac0be68608adf4d20c86450f7c8a024b34a079b94148d0aecb3f52978aa17d", "label": "VERIFIED", "amended_in": "CT-R1-AUDIT/R2"}
{"claim_id": "R1-12", "task_id": "R2-companion", "claim": "The V_quad companion was retrieved from Zenodo concept DOI 10.5281/zenodo.20455089, which resolves to latest record 20481592. Three versions exist, all with title 'A non-classical Painleve V transcendent from a quadratic polynomial continued fraction: surface classification and resurgent Stokes data': v1.0 = 10.5281/zenodo.20455090, 2026-05-30, 538588 bytes, 10 pp, sha256 c07c97d6fcd4d65bb888f951e853c85d21897a55190290fa3e32f38410ff1601; v1.1 = 10.5281/zenodo.20480603, 2026-06-01, 606008 bytes, 12 pp, sha256 e07c1ddab16ffe22e2a118a1f8c97f45c9b959148af01933c9a4a50bc2a790a1; v1.2 = 10.5281/zenodo.20481592, 2026-06-01, 612719 bytes, 12 pp, sha256 a5d9e264699e6397030f0512e17f0cd503fcf2eafd57db9b00b57523fcc88d85. Note the published title differs from the title used in the repo's bibitem{Vquad}, which also cites the v1.0 version DOI rather than the concept DOI.", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "Zenodo REST API + sha256", "output_hash": "89ac0be68608adf4d20c86450f7c8a024b34a079b94148d0aecb3f52978aa17d", "label": "INSPECTED"}
{"claim_id": "R1-13", "task_id": "R2-conj41", "claim": "Object 4.1 across the three companion versions, by regex search of extracted PDF text with fi/fl ligatures normalised: v1.0 has 'Theorem 4.1' (3 occurrences) and no Conjecture 4.1; v1.1 has 'Theorem 4.1' (4 occurrences) and no Conjecture 4.1; v1.2 has 'Conjecture 4.1' (7 occurrences) and no Theorem 4.1. The only other numbered 4.x object anywhere is Remark 4.5 in v1.2. This CONFIRMS the operator's hypothesis exactly: the Conjecture 4.1 label appears only from v1.2, and at v1.0 the object numbered 4.1 is a theorem.", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "pypdf text extraction + regex", "output_hash": "89ac0be68608adf4d20c86450f7c8a024b34a079b94148d0aecb3f52978aa17d", "label": "INSPECTED"}
{"claim_id": "R1-14", "task_id": "R2-conj41-content", "claim": "Conjecture 4.1 is about a THIRD ODE, neither System A nor System B. The companion v1.2 Sec 2.2 derives, by a formal continuum limit of the Wallis recurrence, its equation (6)-(7): a(x)y'' + b(x)y' + c(x)y = 0 with a(x)=3x^2+x+1, b(x)=6x+1, c(x)=-x^2, satisfying the exactness identity b(x)=a'(x) so that the operator is d/dx[a(x)y'] + c(x)y = 0. Call this System C. The companion states its finite singularities are the roots of a(x), namely s_{1,2} = (-1 +- i sqrt 11)/6, both regular singular and ASSERTED APPARENT, and that x=infinity is irregular of Poincare rank 1. Conjecture 4.1 asserts the isomonodromic deformation family containing (6) is governed by Painleve V with alpha=1/6, beta=0, gamma=0, delta=-1/2, with space of initial conditions the Sakai surface D5^(1) and symmetry W(A3^(1)) = affine S4. Note s_{1,2} = (-1 +- i sqrt 11)/6 are exactly the points CT-S5B-COVER computed for the INVERTED System B under z -> 1/x, so System C and the inverted System B are closely related.", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "companion v1.2 Sec 2.2, Remark 2.1, Sec 4", "output_hash": "89ac0be68608adf4d20c86450f7c8a024b34a079b94148d0aecb3f52978aa17d", "label": "INSPECTED"}
{"claim_id": "R1-15", "task_id": "R2-conj41-caveat", "claim": "Conjecture 4.1 documents its own principal weakness, quoted verbatim from companion v1.2 Sec 4: 'the surface-type determination D5^(1) rests on a match against the Jimbo-Miwa-Ueno classification table [5] and is not yet corroborated by an independent Lax-pair derivation (see Remark 4.5).' This matters because van der Put & Saito state in their Introduction (p. 2612) that their work extends Jimbo-Miwa-Ueno precisely by allowing 'all possible irregular singularities including ramification', which the JMU tables exclude. So the conjecture's stated evidential basis is a table that cannot see ramification, which is the very phenomenon at issue in CT-S4. Conjecture 4.1 also argues beta=gamma=0 'reflects the fact that both finite singularities are apparent', making the apparency computation delegated to CT-S6-APPARENCY load-bearing for the conjecture itself.", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "companion v1.2 Sec 4; vdP-Saito p. 2612", "output_hash": "89ac0be68608adf4d20c86450f7c8a024b34a079b94148d0aecb3f52978aa17d", "label": "INSPECTED"}
{"claim_id": "R1-16", "task_id": "R2-taxonomy", "claim": "Operator ruling 1 adopted: new provenance label INSPECTED, with rule (a) any file_inspection claim is INSPECTED and never PROVEN, and rule (b) absence claims phrased 'NOT FOUND in <scope> by <method>'. Applying rule (a) literally would have demoted genuine theorems, because 12 mathematical claims (S1-01..S1-05, S3A-02, S3B-04, S3B-07, R1-02, R1-03, R1-08, R1-09) were tagged evidence_type 'file_inspection' merely because the proof text lives in a .tex or .md file. That is an evidence_type error, not a label error; those are retagged evidence_type='proof' and keep their labels. 16 genuine repository-content claims were relabelled INSPECTED. Three absence claims were rephrased per rule (b). SCHEMA QUESTION FOR THE OPERATOR: 'proof' is a new evidence_type value not in the original file_inspection|computation|build set, introduced as a direct consequence of ruling 1. Please confirm or replace it.", "evidence_type": "computation", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "apply_audit_r2.py", "output_hash": "89ac0be68608adf4d20c86450f7c8a024b34a079b94148d0aecb3f52978aa17d", "label": "STRUCTURAL"}
{"claim_id": "R1-17", "task_id": "CT-R1-AUDIT-R2-VERIFY", "claim": "System C's normal form equals the inverted System B normal form identically, both being (12x^4+4x^3+4x^2+11)/(4(3x^2+x+1)^2); independently re-derived in CT-R1-AUDIT without using CT-S6 outputs.", "label": "PROVEN", "evidence_type": "computation", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "sessions/2026-09-17/CT-R1-AUDIT/verify_s6.py", "output_hash": "c84def82e8b7feb4fcca7bfffbd4df925ebf72249987288c807beb43830e442b"}
{"claim_id": "R1-18", "task_id": "CT-R1-AUDIT-R2-VERIFY", "claim": "At every simple root s of chi, the equation chi*y'' + chi'*y' + c*y = 0 has p = chi'/chi with residue exactly 1 and q = c/chi with at most a simple pole, so (x-s)^2*q -> 0 and the indicial polynomial is exactly lambda^2 REGARDLESS OF THE VALUE OF c(s). The exponents are therefore 0,0, equal exponents at a regular singular point always force a log term in the second Frobenius solution, and the point is never apparent. This refutes companion Remark 2.2 in full generality.", "label": "PROVEN", "evidence_type": "computation", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "sessions/2026-09-17/CT-R1-AUDIT/verify_s6.py", "output_hash": "c84def82e8b7feb4fcca7bfffbd4df925ebf72249987288c807beb43830e442b", "claim_before_r3": "At every simple root s of chi with c(s)!=0, the equation chi*y''+chi'*y'+c*y=0 has indicial polynomial exactly lambda^2, so the exponents are 0,0 and the point is never apparent; this refutes companion Remark 2.2 in full generality rather than by counterexample.", "audit_r3": "Operator review #3, correction A: the hypothesis c(s) != 0 is unnecessary and has been dropped. Once p has residue 1 and q has at most a simple pole, the indicial polynomial is lambda^2 whatever c(s) is; equal exponents then force the log term. The lemma is strictly more general than first recorded.", "amended_in": "CT-R1-AUDIT/R3", "review": "cold", "audit_r7": "Cold-read SOUND by CT-S11-COLDREAD3 from a self-contained packet with no access to the derivation history. The cold reader also IMPROVED the proof: instead of appealing generically to Frobenius theory for the log term, it gave the explicit reduction-of-order argument. Since p = chi'/chi, exp(-int p) = 1/chi, so the second solution is y2 = y1 * int dx/(chi*y1^2), whose integrand has a simple pole at s with residue 1/(h(s)*y1(s)^2) != 0. This exhibits the log coefficient EXPLICITLY and nonzero, closing the only soft step. Confirmed by hand. It also confirmed that dropping c(s) != 0 is legitimate and that the phrase 'assume s is a genuine singular point' does no hidden work, since p is singular at any simple root of chi regardless of c.", "review_note": "proof: CT-S11-COLDREAD3 read a self-contained packet (coldpackets/PACKET-A) with no access to the derivation history, and improved the proof by supplying the explicit reduction-of-order argument for the nonzero log coefficient."}
{"claim_id": "R1-19", "task_id": "CT-R1-AUDIT-R2-VERIFY", "claim": "System C at s_pm=(-1 +/- i*sqrt(11))/6 has normal-form residue -1/4, hence a repeated exponent 1/2, hence a log term: NOT APPARENT. The companion's claimed exponents {0,1} with theta_1=theta_2=0 are refuted.", "label": "PROVEN", "evidence_type": "computation", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "sessions/2026-09-17/CT-R1-AUDIT/verify_s6.py", "output_hash": "c84def82e8b7feb4fcca7bfffbd4df925ebf72249987288c807beb43830e442b"}
{"claim_id": "R1-20", "task_id": "CT-R1-AUDIT-R2-VERIFY", "claim": "System B's point z=infinity has local exponents differing by exactly 1 and no log term, and becomes an ordinary point of the normal form (R = 11/4, finite, at x=0 under z=1/x). UP TO A RANK-1 TWIST it therefore carries no moduli, and System B's effective Katz multiset is (0,0,1) rather than (1,0,0,0). This is equivalence up to a rank-1 twist, NOT equivalence of the operators themselves; it is valid for reading van der Put-Saito Table 2.1 because that table classifies trace-free rank-2 connections, which is exactly the up-to-twist setting. CT-S6 claim S6-C7 is SUPERSEDED as an artefact of an apparency test that disallows twisting.", "label": "STRUCTURAL", "evidence_type": "computation", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "sessions/2026-09-17/CT-R1-AUDIT/verify_s6.py", "output_hash": "c84def82e8b7feb4fcca7bfffbd4df925ebf72249987288c807beb43830e442b", "claim_before_r3": "System B's point z=infinity has exponents differing by exactly 1 and becomes an ordinary point of the normal form (R=11/4 finite at x=0 under z=1/x), so it carries no moduli; System B's effective Katz multiset after rank-1 normalisation is (0,0,1), not (1,0,0,0). CT-S6 claim S6-C7 is SUPERSEDED as an artefact of an apparency test that disallows twisting.", "audit_r3": "Operator review #3, correction B: claim text must say 'up to twist'. 'Ordinary after twist' is equivalence up to a rank-1 twist, not equivalence of the operators themselves. That is the setting Table 2.1 uses (trace-free rank-2 connections), so the (0,0,1) reading is valid there.", "amended_in": "CT-R1-AUDIT/R3", "review": "cold", "review_note": "cold-confirmed by CT-S14-COLDREAD-B on its central assertion, that z=infinity is not a genuine extra singular point and the tuple is (0,0,1) (see R1-74); CT-S14 reached it independently under isolation."}
{"claim_id": "R1-21", "task_id": "CT-R1-AUDIT-R2-VERIFY", "claim": "Conjecture 4.1's conclusion (Sakai surface D5^(1), PV) is consistent with the van der Put-Saito Table 2.1 row (0,0,1) p.2635 for System C, but its stated reason is false because the finite singularities are not apparent; and a matching Katz multiset is necessary but not sufficient for family membership.", "label": "STRUCTURAL", "evidence_type": "computation", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "sessions/2026-09-17/CT-R1-AUDIT/verify_s6.py", "output_hash": "c84def82e8b7feb4fcca7bfffbd4df925ebf72249987288c807beb43830e442b"}
{"claim_id": "R1-22", "task_id": "CT-R1-AUDIT-R3", "claim": "The stale bibitem{Vquad} is in the PERIOD-REP paper, not in Channel Theory. It was ALREADY CORRECTED in the 2026-06-16 layout-fix cascade: VQUAD-PAPER-CORRECTIONS-001, VQUAD-PAPER-LAYOUTFIX-001 and VQUAD-REPRO-BUNDLE-002 (both slot-root and run-2) all carry the actual Zenodo title 'A non-classical Painleve V transcendent from a quadratic polynomial continued fraction: surface classification and resurgent Stokes data' and the CONCEPT DOI 10.5281/zenodo.20455089. The stale form, citing version DOI 10.5281/zenodo.20455090 with the old title, survives only in the superseded 2026-06-15 VQUAD-PERIODREP-PAPER-001 draft and in the superseded VQUAD-REPRO-BUNDLE-001 copy. CT-S4 read the 2026-06-15 draft. The deposit-ready path VQUAD-REPRO-BUNDLE-002/run-2 is correct, so no fix is required.", "label": "INSPECTED", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "sessions/2026-09-17/CT-R1-AUDIT/apply_audit_r3.py", "output_hash": null}
