{"claim_id": "R1-29", "task_id": "CT-R1-AUDIT-R5", "claim": "The Jimbo PV dictionary quoted by CT-S9 is transcribed EXACTLY from Jimbo, 'Monodromy Problem and the Boundary Condition for Some Painleve Equations', PRIMS, p.1152: alpha=(1/8)(th0-tht+thinf)^2, beta=-(1/8)(th0-tht-thinf)^2, gamma=1-th0-tht, delta=-1/2, with eigenvalues of A_nu equal to +/- th_nu/2 so that the exponent difference at nu is exactly th_nu. Verified by reading the page image in CT-S9-PVPARAMS/outputs/jimbo_page16-16.png.", "label": "INSPECTED", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "sessions/2026-09-17/CT-R1-AUDIT/verify_s9.py", "output_hash": null}
{"claim_id": "R1-30", "task_id": "CT-R1-AUDIT-R5", "claim": "CT-S9's System C computation reproduces independently: normal form (12x^4+4x^3+4x^2+11)/(4(3x^2+x+1)^2), residue -1/4 and exponent difference 0 at both s_pm, R->1/3 at infinity with WKB exponentials exp(+/- sqrt(3)x/3). Hence th0=tht=0 and the Jimbo dictionary gives alpha=thinf^2/8, beta=-alpha, gamma=1, delta=-1/2.", "label": "PROVEN", "evidence_type": "computation", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "sessions/2026-09-17/CT-R1-AUDIT/verify_s9.py", "output_hash": "8d701a05e5de246c66ad703436f28a17a95234d8217ab7e309ac40dd562e8772"}
{"claim_id": "R1-31", "task_id": "CT-R1-AUDIT-R5", "claim": "The contradiction with the companion's gamma=0 is genuine, not a convention artefact: under the PV scaling z -> c*z the parameters transform as (alpha,beta,gamma,delta) -> (alpha,beta,c*gamma,c^2*delta), so holding delta=-1/2 forces c=+/-1 and gamma is fixed up to sign. gamma=1 cannot be rescaled to gamma=0.", "label": "PROVEN", "evidence_type": "computation", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "sessions/2026-09-17/CT-R1-AUDIT/verify_s9.py", "output_hash": "8d701a05e5de246c66ad703436f28a17a95234d8217ab7e309ac40dd562e8772", "review": "cold", "audit_r7": "Cold-read SOUND by CT-S12-COLDREAD4, which re-derived the PV rescaling law from the Painleve V equation by direct symbolic substitution rather than taking it on trust -- the single load-bearing step. It confirmed (alpha,beta,gamma,delta) -> (alpha,beta,c*gamma,c^2*delta) for W(z)=w(cz), AND checked the opposite convention, where it reads (alpha,beta,gamma/c,delta/c^2). The conclusion holds under either: fixing delta = -1/2 forces c^2 = 1, so gamma = 1 cannot be rescaled to gamma = 0.", "review_note": "computation: CT-S12-COLDREAD4 re-derived the PV rescaling law from the Painleve V equation by direct symbolic substitution in its OWN SymPy script (compute_pv_checks.py), with no access to verify_s9.py or verify_s9.out, and additionally checked the opposite scaling convention. Different code, same conclusion."}
{"claim_id": "R1-32", "task_id": "CT-R1-AUDIT-R5", "claim": "Jimbo's standing assumption (A1)_PV, 'th0, tht not in Z', stated on the same page immediately below the dictionary, is VIOLATED by System C's local data, which gives th0=tht=0 in Z. CT-S9 did not flag this. The dictionary itself precedes (A1)_PV and is unconditional, so the parameter computation stands; but everything Jimbo derives after that line is outside its stated hypotheses for this case. Coherence check: integer theta is precisely the resonant case, and resonance is precisely when logs can appear -- logs were independently found at both finite points.", "label": "INSPECTED", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "sessions/2026-09-17/CT-R1-AUDIT/verify_s9.py", "output_hash": null, "review": "cold", "audit_r7": "Independently rediscovered by CT-S12-COLDREAD4 directly from the Jimbo page image, without being told to look for it: the page states the standing assumption (A1)_PV 'theta_0, theta_t not in Z', which the case theta_0 = theta_t = 0 violates. Two independent parties have now found this on the page. CT-S9-PVPARAMS, which produced the original result, missed it.", "review_note": "computation/inspection: CT-S12-COLDREAD4 read the Jimbo page image itself and independently rediscovered the (A1)_PV assumption without being prompted to look for it. Independent observation of the same primary source, not a re-run."}
{"claim_id": "R1-33", "task_id": "CT-R1-AUDIT-R5", "claim": "The PV time for System C is NOT a free deformation parameter; it is FIXED. Jimbo's system (3.1) normalises the irregular part at infinity to exp(x*diag(1,0)), whose exponent difference is exactly x. System C's exponent difference at infinity is 2*sqrt(3)x/3, so the affine scale k=2/sqrt(3) is forced, and t = k*(s_mp - s_pm) = -/+ 2i*sqrt(33)/9 with |t| = 2*sqrt(33)/9. System C therefore corresponds to a SINGLE value of the PV time (the two signs differing only by relabelling s+ and s-). A membership claim would require exhibiting a curve t -> L_t of connections, isomonodromic in t, whose fibre at t = -/+ 2i*sqrt(33)/9 is System C; such a family was NOT FOUND in the inspected sources by the methods used.", "label": "STRUCTURAL", "evidence_type": "computation", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "sessions/2026-09-17/CT-R1-AUDIT/verify_s9.py", "output_hash": "8d701a05e5de246c66ad703436f28a17a95234d8217ab7e309ac40dd562e8772", "review": "cold", "audit_r7": "Cold-read SOUND WITH CAVEAT by CT-S12-COLDREAD4. It confirmed that k = 2/sqrt(3) is forced by Jimbo's normalisation at infinity and that t = -/+ 2i*sqrt(33)/9 follows, so the operator is a single normalised fibre. CAVEAT, independently raised and matching the flag already on this claim: the identification of the two finite singular points with Jimbo's 0 and t is an ASSUMPTION, legitimate for placing a two-finite-singularity one-irregular-singularity problem into Jimbo's normalisation but not proved by the scalar equation alone. The conclusion is conditional on it.", "review_note": "computation: CT-S12-COLDREAD4 recomputed k and t in its own script from the packet statement, with no access to verify_s9.py. Verdict SOUND WITH CAVEAT; the caveat (the affine identification is an assumption) was raised independently."}
{"claim_id": "R1-34", "task_id": "CT-R1-AUDIT-R5", "claim": "Net position on companion Conjecture 4.1 after CT-S9 and its audit: alpha=1/6 UNDETERMINED by local data (alpha=thinf^2/8 and thinf is not fixed by local scalar data); beta=0 CONTRADICTED jointly with alpha=1/6 since beta=-alpha identically; gamma=0 CONTRADICTED since gamma=1 and is not rescalable; delta=-1/2 CONSISTENT as Jimbo's normalisation. The 'right row, wrong reason' position hardens: the (0,0,1) Katz multiset still matches the van der Put-Saito D5/PV row p.2635, but the parameter tuple attached to it does not survive the correct local data.", "label": "STRUCTURAL", "evidence_type": "computation", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "sessions/2026-09-17/CT-R1-AUDIT/verify_s9.py", "output_hash": "8d701a05e5de246c66ad703436f28a17a95234d8217ab7e309ac40dd562e8772"}
{"claim_id": "R1-35", "task_id": "CT-R1-AUDIT-R5", "claim": "Deposit gate 1 is CLOSED. Both target passages of theorem.tex have now been cold-read by independent sessions with no access to their derivation history: thm:radius Step 3 SOUND (CT-S7-COLDREAD), and thm:growth Step 3 / G1 SOUND after repair (CT-S10-COLDREAD2). Two defects were found and fixed in the process: a misquoted DLMF equation number and a stale DLMF release string. Claims S1-03 and S1-04 both now carry review='cold'. Gate 2 (no machine-checked claim) remains OPEN by design: 7 sorry's remain in XiZero.lean. Gate 3 (prior art) is still delegated to CT-S8-LITCHECK and NOT returned.", "label": "INSPECTED", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "sessions/2026-09-17/CT-R1-AUDIT/verify_s9.py", "output_hash": null}
{"claim_id": "R1-36", "task_id": "CT-R1-AUDIT-R6", "claim": "Gautschi, SIAM Review 9(1) 1967, hypothesis (2.8) on journal p.34 reads EXACTLY: 'a_n ~ a n^alpha, b_n ~ b n^beta, ab != 0; alpha, beta real; n -> infinity', with Newton-Puiseux points P0(0,0), P1(1,alpha), P2(2,beta). The reality condition is on the EXPONENTS, not on the coefficients. Verified by re-rendering the page from the PDF at 3x (refs/gautschi_p34_bot.png) because the OCR layer rendered this as 'ab 0; a, real', which would have wrongly suggested the leading coefficient must be real and hence that Perron-Kreuser does not cover complex beta_d. It does cover it.", "label": "INSPECTED", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "sessions/2026-09-17/CT-R1-AUDIT/VERIFY-S8.md", "output_hash": "e6728427ef0bb80c16d30c9cf260134f2027fdb07befedb1ccfebd678b28f468"}
{"claim_id": "R1-37", "task_id": "CT-R1-AUDIT-R6", "claim": "Result 1 (the radius / nth-root theorem, theorem.tex part (i)) is PRIOR ART: it is a corollary of the Perron-Kreuser theorem as stated in Gautschi Theorem 2.3(a), p.35. Writing Q_{n+1} - b(n+1)Q_n - Q_{n-1} = 0 in Gautschi's form (2.1) gives a_n ~ -beta_d n^d and b_n = -1, so alpha=d, beta=0, hypotheses (2.2) and (2.8) hold, and P1(1,d) lies above the segment (0,0)-(2,0) for every d >= 1, so case (a) applies and Q_{n+1}/Q_n ~ beta_d n^d. Stirling then gives |Q_n/(dn)!|^(1/n) -> |beta_d|/d^d. CT-S8-LITCHECK's finding is CONFIRMED by independent re-derivation from the verified page images.", "label": "STRUCTURAL", "evidence_type": "computation", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "sessions/2026-09-17/CT-R1-AUDIT/VERIFY-S8.md", "output_hash": "e6728427ef0bb80c16d30c9cf260134f2027fdb07befedb1ccfebd678b28f468"}
{"claim_id": "R1-38", "task_id": "CT-R1-AUDIT-R6", "claim": "The decomposition of Result 1 into classical parts is complete, leaving no new residue: Perron-Kreuser supplies the ratio law for the dominant solution and applies to our recurrence UNCONDITIONALLY (it needs no analogue of (H)); hypothesis (H) is exactly the statement that Q_n is not the minimal solution, which is Pincherle's theorem (Gautschi Thm 1.1 p.31, DLMF 3.6(ii)); and the passage from the ratio law to the radius is routine Stirling.", "label": "STRUCTURAL", "evidence_type": "computation", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "sessions/2026-09-17/CT-R1-AUDIT/VERIFY-S8.md", "output_hash": "e6728427ef0bb80c16d30c9cf260134f2027fdb07befedb1ccfebd678b28f468"}
{"claim_id": "R1-39", "task_id": "CT-R1-AUDIT-R6", "claim": "Whether the explicit growth exponent s = beta_{d-1}/beta_d + (d-1)/2 is already in print is NOT ESTABLISHED. DLMF 2.9 gives explicit exponents only for bounded coefficients and explicitly defers the case of eq. 2.9.14 (ours: P=d, Q=0) to Wong & Li, Stud. Appl. Math. 87(4) 1992, 289-324, which is paywalled (Wiley HTTP 403) and was NOT OBTAINED. Recorded as NOT FOUND in the sources obtained by the methods used, NOT as new. This is the single blocking item for deposit gate 3 and cannot be closed from open sources; it requires operator action.", "label": "INSPECTED", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "sessions/2026-09-17/CT-R1-AUDIT/VERIFY-S8.md", "output_hash": null}
{"claim_id": "R1-40", "task_id": "CT-R1-AUDIT-R6", "claim": "CT-S8-LITCHECK independently derived and numerically verified (60 dps, N=4000, four polynomials d=1,2,3) the closed form K = r_inf (2pi)^((d-1)/2) / (sqrt(d) prod_i Gamma(1-r_i)), reproducing P3's amplitude without access to P3's derivation. This materially strengthens the K result at the same time as Result 1 is demoted.", "label": "VERIFIED", "evidence_type": "computation", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "sessions/2026-09-17/CT-R1-AUDIT/VERIFY-S8.md", "output_hash": null, "review": "cold", "review_note": "computation: CT-S8-LITCHECK derived K independently from the Gauss multiplication formula and verified it numerically at 60 dps, N=4000, for four polynomials (d=1,2,3), using its own script (scripts/verify_growth_law.py) with no access to P3's derivation, script or output. Different code and an independently motivated derivation, so this meets the `cold` bar for computations."}
{"claim_id": "R1-41", "task_id": "CT-R1-AUDIT-R6", "claim": "The NOT FOUND verdict on K carries less weight than it appears to, pending R1-39. Result 1 was found to be classical only once the search term 'Perron-Kreuser' surfaced, and Wong & Li -- the source most likely to contain Result 2 and plausibly related to K -- was never read. The K novelty claim should not be relied upon until the Wong & Li gap is closed.", "label": "STRUCTURAL", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "sessions/2026-09-17/CT-R1-AUDIT/VERIFY-S8.md", "output_hash": null}
{"claim_id": "R1-42", "task_id": "CT-R1-AUDIT-R6", "claim": "Deposit gate 3 is RETURNED but NOT CLOSED. The note's contribution claim as drafted is no longer supportable: Result 1 must be presented as a corollary of Perron-Kreuser with attribution, Result 2's status is undetermined pending Wong & Li, and Result 3 (K) is the strongest remaining candidate. The vacuity explanation is unaffected and was NOT FOUND in the literature searched.", "label": "INSPECTED", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "sessions/2026-09-17/CT-R1-AUDIT/VERIFY-S8.md", "output_hash": null}
{"claim_id": "R1-43", "task_id": "CT-R1-AUDIT-R7", "claim": "Cold read A (CT-S11-COLDREAD3) returns SOUND on the Remark 2.2 lemma, and strengthens it. Its explicit reduction-of-order argument gives the logarithm's coefficient as 1/(h(s) y1(s)^2), manifestly nonzero, replacing the packet's generic appeal to Frobenius theory. Verified by hand: with p = chi'/chi, exp(-int p dx) = 1/chi, so the reduction-of-order integrand is 1/(chi y1^2), which has a simple pole at any simple root s of chi. This is now the recommended form of the proof.", "label": "PROVEN", "evidence_type": "proof", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "sessions/2026-09-17/CT-R1-AUDIT/coldpackets/", "output_hash": "e8e1a9128587293b3c765a438c47c6fe242b1c6d6dcfdf659a1d0712c26a0d5d", "review": "cold", "review_note": "proof: as R1-18; this claim records the improvement itself."}
{"claim_id": "R1-44", "task_id": "CT-R1-AUDIT-R7", "claim": "Cold read B (CT-S12-COLDREAD4) returns SOUND WITH CAVEAT on the PV parameter contradiction. The two caveats are (a) the published tuple (1/6,0,0,-1/2) was unsourced IN THE PACKET -- an artefact of cold-read design, since the packet deliberately withheld the companion paper to preserve isolation; the tuple is sourced in the repo -- and (b) the (A1)_PV violation, which was already recorded as R1-32. Neither caveat is a new defect.", "label": "INSPECTED", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "sessions/2026-09-17/CT-R1-AUDIT/coldpackets/", "output_hash": "270301c660c5726bf7c0df49ba383cb34cb4ab9931c5336c365fde8f2eddc592"}
{"claim_id": "R1-45", "task_id": "CT-R1-AUDIT-R7", "claim": "DLMF bibliography verified 2026-09-17 at https://dlmf.nist.gov/bib/W: 'Wong and Li (1992a)' is 'Asymptotic expansions for second-order linear difference equations. II', Stud. Appl. Math. 87(4) 289-324, and it is the entry cited for eq. (2.9.14) -- our case. 'Wong and Li (1992b)' is J. Comput. Appl. Math. 41(1-2) 65-94, cited for the bounded-coefficient case, which is NOT ours. CT-S8-LITCHECK's identification is CONFIRMED. The suffix ordering is counterintuitive -- '1992a' is the paper titled 'II' -- so any access request must quote the full citation, not the DLMF key.", "label": "INSPECTED", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "sessions/2026-09-17/CT-R1-AUDIT/coldpackets/", "output_hash": "2a90b9f01153541fe38f804d5ef07a3274d565cd8672e81e9c9a91cc5dab640d"}
{"claim_id": "R1-46", "task_id": "CT-R1-AUDIT-R7", "claim": "Wong & Li (1992a) was NOT OBTAINED. The Wiley copy is paywalled; no mirror or shadow library was used. The DOI for the companion paper Wong & Li (1992b) resolves to a ScienceDirect stub reporting accessType anon_guest, which is not evidence of open access and is in any case the wrong paper. Access requires operator action: Wiley single-article purchase, National Diet Library or university visitor access to Stud. Appl. Math. 1992 holdings, or an author request.", "label": "INSPECTED", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "sessions/2026-09-17/CT-R1-AUDIT/coldpackets/", "output_hash": null}
{"claim_id": "R1-47", "task_id": "CT-R1-AUDIT-R7", "claim": "Deposit route CHANGED by operator review #4: the standalone note is DROPPED. The residual contribution after gate 3 is too thin to carry a note -- K is a routine product-of-Gammas computation given the growth law, its substance sits in r_inf which has no closed form (PSLQ null), and in the Birkhoff-Trjitzinsky / Wong-Li framework the constant multiplying the dominant solution is exactly the undetermined connection constant; the Borel framing and the vacuity explanation are expository. The material goes into Channel Theory v1.7 as a correction-and-attribution notice instead, which also removes the Wong-Li blocker, since a version notice can state plainly that the question was not determined whereas a note claiming a contribution could not.", "label": "INSPECTED", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "sessions/2026-09-17/CT-R1-AUDIT/coldpackets/", "output_hash": null}
{"claim_id": "R1-48", "task_id": "CT-R1-AUDIT-R7", "claim": "Two notice drafts prepared for the operator, neither applied to any source file: DRAFT-CT-v1.7-NOTICE.md (items N1-N4: attribution of Conjecture 3.3.A* to Perron-Kreuser plus Pincherle and retirement of the conjecture label; supersession of the EBR positivity grounding; K and the r_inf series; the one-line vacuity explanation) and DRAFT-COMPANION-v1.3-NOTICE.md (items C1-C4: the Remark 2.2 lemma; the refuted derivation and the genuine parameter contradiction; the well-posedness restatement of Conjecture 4.1; the per-object label table). Passages whose wording depends on Wong & Li are marked [WONG-LI] with two alternative phrasings each.", "label": "INSPECTED", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "sessions/2026-09-17/CT-R1-AUDIT/coldpackets/", "output_hash": null}
{"claim_id": "R1-49", "task_id": "CT-R1-AUDIT-R7", "claim": "Citation hygiene adopted as a standing P0 rule (P0-CITATION-RULE.md): re-fetch and hash every external citation at deposit time; read rendered page images rather than OCR for any load-bearing statement; the rule covers HYPOTHESES as well as theorem statements; never use a mirror or shadow library for a paywalled source. Evidence base: four citation-level defects in this run, none in any mathematical argument, one of which (the Gautschi (2.8) OCR artefact, in a hypothesis) would have flipped the prior-art conclusion.", "label": "INSPECTED", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "sessions/2026-09-17/CT-R1-AUDIT/coldpackets/", "output_hash": null}
{"claim_id": "R1-61", "task_id": "CT-R1-AUDIT-R8", "claim": "The Wong-Li title in the operator's draft author request was defective: it read 'Asymptotic expansions for second-order difference equations, II', omitting the word 'linear'. Both the publisher record (Crossref, DOI 10.1002/sapm1992874289) and the stored DLMF bibliography (refs/dlmf_bib_W.html) give 'second-order LINEAR difference equations'. Corrected in both the subject line and the body. Aggravating factor: DLMF 1992b carries the same title minus the trailing 'II', so a degraded title can resolve to the wrong paper.", "label": "INSPECTED", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "gate1_locate.py / apply_audit_r8.py", "output_hash": "f14109cc8187685d7994b767b1ad611847e35b0286eb1406d06e6f1ca9b009c3", "review": "self", "review_note": "self: produced and checked by this session. Gate 1 was specified by the operator as a NON-isolated check, so `self` is the correct and intended value here, not a shortfall.", "renumbered_from": "R1-44", "renumber_note": "Renumbered during R9. The R8 batch collided with six R7 claim_ids; the R7 occurrences keep the original numbers and these R8 occurrences were moved to free numbers. No claim content changed."}
{"claim_id": "R1-62", "task_id": "CT-R1-AUDIT-R8", "claim": "The signature block of the author request (mononym 'Papanokechi', ORCID 0009-0000-6192-8273, Yokohama) was verified character by character, ORCID digit by digit, against sessions/2026-06-16/VQUAD-ZENODO-DEPOSIT-001/upload-copy-paste.md. It matches. No part of the identity block was invented.", "label": "INSPECTED", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "gate1_locate.py / apply_audit_r8.py", "output_hash": "f14109cc8187685d7994b767b1ad611847e35b0286eb1406d06e6f1ca9b009c3", "review": "self", "review_note": "self: produced and checked by this session. Gate 1 was specified by the operator as a NON-isolated check, so `self` is the correct and intended value here, not a shortfall.", "renumbered_from": "R1-45", "renumber_note": "Renumbered during R9. The R8 batch collided with six R7 claim_ids; the R7 occurrences keep the original numbers and these R8 occurrences were moved to free numbers. No claim content changed."}
{"claim_id": "R1-63", "task_id": "CT-R1-AUDIT-R8", "claim": "GATE 1 PASS. Every tuple, equation number and remark number quoted in DRAFT-COMPANION-v1.3-NOTICE.md was checked against companion v1.2 (sha256 a5d9e264...) by locating the pages and then reading 3x-rendered page images per the P0 rule. All 11 checked items match, including Remark 2.2's number and verbatim apparency wording, Conjecture 4.1's number, and the tuple (alpha,beta,gamma,delta) = (1/6, 0, 0, -1/2). No defect found.", "label": "INSPECTED", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "gate1_locate.py / apply_audit_r8.py", "output_hash": "16a56ed8bd49b0c2213e66b2f9a1a90d40faf717eae02623550aac8fe45cffe7", "review": "self", "review_note": "self: produced and checked by this session. Gate 1 was specified by the operator as a NON-isolated check, so `self` is the correct and intended value here, not a shortfall.", "renumbered_from": "R1-46", "renumber_note": "Renumbered during R9. The R8 batch collided with six R7 claim_ids; the R7 occurrences keep the original numbers and these R8 occurrences were moved to free numbers. No claim content changed."}
{"claim_id": "R1-64", "task_id": "CT-R1-AUDIT-R8", "claim": "Companion v1.2 p.6 states and applies the PV scaling law (alpha,beta,gamma,delta) -> (alpha,beta,c*gamma,c^2*delta) with c=sqrt(3), to send delta_raw=-1/6 to delta=-1/2. This is the SAME law used in our refutation, so the 'convention artefact' defence of gamma=0 is closed by the companion's own text. Its assertion that the rescaling leaves gamma=0 invariant holds only because gamma was assumed 0; the correct value gamma=1 maps to sqrt(3).", "label": "INSPECTED", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "gate1_locate.py / apply_audit_r8.py", "output_hash": "16a56ed8bd49b0c2213e66b2f9a1a90d40faf717eae02623550aac8fe45cffe7", "review": "self", "review_note": "self: produced and checked by this session. Gate 1 was specified by the operator as a NON-isolated check, so `self` is the correct and intended value here, not a shortfall.", "renumbered_from": "R1-47", "renumber_note": "Renumbered during R9. The R8 batch collided with six R7 claim_ids; the R7 occurrences keep the original numbers and these R8 occurrences were moved to free numbers. No claim content changed."}
{"claim_id": "R1-65", "task_id": "CT-R1-AUDIT-R8", "claim": "The gamma contradiction does not depend on the C1 apparency lemma. The companion's own assignment theta_1 = theta_2 = 0 is CORRECT as a statement about local exponents; Jimbo's dictionary gamma = 1 - theta_0 - theta_t then yields gamma = 1, so the published gamma = 0 is unattainable on the companion's own local data. C1 is load-bearing only for the monodromy statement (unipotent, nontrivial) and for Remark 2.2 itself. C2 therefore has two independent grounds.", "label": "PROVEN", "evidence_type": "proof", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "gate1_locate.py / apply_audit_r8.py", "output_hash": "d62968358652cd831524416075219f41972fff85dedd28583e9dfe7c6921b02a", "review": "self", "review_note": "self: produced and checked by this session. Gate 1 was specified by the operator as a NON-isolated check, so `self` is the correct and intended value here, not a shortfall.", "renumbered_from": "R1-48", "renumber_note": "Renumbered during R9. The R8 batch collided with six R7 claim_ids; the R7 occurrences keep the original numbers and these R8 occurrences were moved to free numbers. No claim content changed."}
{"claim_id": "R1-66", "task_id": "CT-R1-AUDIT-R8", "claim": "A full-text pass over companion v1.2 located five passages depending on the apparency claim, now tabulated as section C5 of the draft notice. The substantive one is Sec 7.1 item 1, which offers apparency as the first of four components of a 'complete explanation' for the identification obstruction; it must be withdrawn or re-argued. The other three components are unaffected, the theta_1=theta_2=0 degeneration of the Jimbo connection formula in particular, since those exponent values are correct.", "label": "INSPECTED", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "gate1_locate.py / apply_audit_r8.py", "output_hash": "16a56ed8bd49b0c2213e66b2f9a1a90d40faf717eae02623550aac8fe45cffe7", "review": "self", "review_note": "self: produced and checked by this session. Gate 1 was specified by the operator as a NON-isolated check, so `self` is the correct and intended value here, not a shortfall.", "renumbered_from": "R1-49", "renumber_note": "Renumbered during R9. The R8 batch collided with six R7 claim_ids; the R7 occurrences keep the original numbers and these R8 occurrences were moved to free numbers. No claim content changed."}
{"claim_id": "R1-50", "task_id": "CT-R1-AUDIT-R8", "claim": "GATE 3 (wording): one defect found and fixed. 'Necessary condition' language is present on every row match (C4 point 1, reinforced by points 2-4): PASS. C3 was NOT verbatim as drafted -- it read 'The operator has the local formal type...' where the operator's drafted text names the object, 'System C has the local formal type...'. This is exactly the per-object ambiguity C4 forbids, and 'operator' is overloaded in this repository. Corrected to 'System C'.", "label": "INSPECTED", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "gate1_locate.py / apply_audit_r8.py", "output_hash": "665a49de02d05e16d488b6e597e5263aea6ff5f737614195c79b2fbfa4fc2e65", "review": "self", "review_note": "self: produced and checked by this session. Gate 1 was specified by the operator as a NON-isolated check, so `self` is the correct and intended value here, not a shortfall."}
{"claim_id": "R1-51", "task_id": "CT-R1-AUDIT-R8", "claim": "RULING 2 APPLIED: the `review` field now defines `cold` per claim type. Proofs: read by an independent party without the derivation history. Computations: reproduced by an independent party using DIFFERENT CODE, ideally a different method, without access to the original script or output; re-executing the original script stays `self`. Every review value now carries a `review_note` recording the method. Retro-applied across 36 reviewed claims: 8 cold, 28 self, 0 lacking a review_note. R1-40 (CT-S8's independent 60-dps derivation and verification of K from the Gauss multiplication formula, own script) was promoted to cold under the new definition.", "label": "INSPECTED", "evidence_type": "build", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "gate1_locate.py / apply_audit_r8.py", "output_hash": "02c2e40ddbd2cb04ed8ad0c33b32fb4e10b8695c838c7fb7d995396b5f3b4e40", "review": "self", "review_note": "self: produced and checked by this session. Gate 1 was specified by the operator as a NON-isolated check, so `self` is the correct and intended value here, not a shortfall."}
{"claim_id": "R1-52", "task_id": "CT-R1-AUDIT-R8", "claim": "GATE 2 RESULT. Cold read of C4 returns: (A0)-(A3) and (A5) SOUND (Katz 1/2 at 0 and infinity, ramified, both doubled to 1 and unramified on the quadratic cover; the ODE annihilates the series, verified to z^43 in independent code); the Table 2.1 row lookups to PIII(D8) and PIII(D6) are correct as ordered Katz-data matches; but (A6) is ERROR as a family-membership inference.", "label": "STRUCTURAL", "evidence_type": "computation", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "CT-S13-COLDREAD5/compute_system_a.py", "output_hash": "610b420f55d319204bc8397ffadf8123e7368c8eed0419dbaa5f04f64846d090", "review": "cold", "review_note": "cold: CT-S13-COLDREAD5 worked from a self-contained packet with no access to CT-S4-FORMAL-TYPE, CT-S5B-COVER, CLASSIFICATION-TABLE.md, any DRAFT-*, VERIFY-*, AUDIT.md or REPORT.md. It recomputed the Katz data in its own SymPy script (compute_system_a.py) and read Table 2.1 from the rendered page images, not an OCR layer. Different code and independent reading of the primary source."}
{"claim_id": "R1-53", "task_id": "CT-R1-AUDIT-R8", "claim": "NEW DEFECT FOUND BY GATE 2, independently re-verified by this session from the PDF: van der Put-Saito p.2634 states that the strong Riemann-Hilbert problem has a positive answer for every type EXCEPT possibly (1/2,-,1/2) and (-,-,5/2), and that for those two types they consider only the modules M(u) for which it does hold. (1/2,-,1/2) is exactly object A's type. The PIII(D8) row is therefore restricted by a condition that has NOT been checked for object A. Written into the notice as C4 point 5.", "label": "INSPECTED", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "CT-S13-COLDREAD5/compute_system_a.py", "output_hash": "61fa0278fc0ec35d88746b55823f88211ee9fe1626250fa4c39350fa3fc91eb2", "review": "cold", "review_note": "cold: CT-S13-COLDREAD5 worked from a self-contained packet with no access to CT-S4-FORMAL-TYPE, CT-S5B-COVER, CLASSIFICATION-TABLE.md, any DRAFT-*, VERIFY-*, AUDIT.md or REPORT.md. It recomputed the Katz data in its own SymPy script (compute_system_a.py) and read Table 2.1 from the rendered page images, not an OCR layer. Different code and independent reading of the primary source."}
{"claim_id": "R1-54", "task_id": "CT-R1-AUDIT-R8", "claim": "The three-entry notation (1/2,-,1/2) is van der Put-Saito's OWN designation for the family, not a contraction introduced in this work: p.2634 reads 'We will not number these ten families, but indicate them by their Katz invariants, e.g., (0,0,0,0), (0,0,1), ..., (0,-,3/2), (-,-,3), (-,-,5/2).' The cold reader's Q5 caveat that the notation suppresses table columns is therefore not accepted on its premise, though its ordered-column point is correct and has been adopted.", "label": "INSPECTED", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "CT-S13-COLDREAD5/compute_system_a.py", "output_hash": "61fa0278fc0ec35d88746b55823f88211ee9fe1626250fa4c39350fa3fc91eb2", "review": "self", "review_note": "self: resolved by this session from the running text on the same page; the isolated reader was right to flag the apparent mismatch."}
{"claim_id": "R1-55", "task_id": "CT-R1-AUDIT-R8", "claim": "C4 weakened and re-grounded in response to gate 2. Added: point 1 now quotes the caption 'Classification of Families' and the trace-zero rank-2 setup from p.2634; point 5 the strong Riemann-Hilbert restriction; point 6 the unbridged scalar-operator-to-rank-2-connection gap (determinant condition, irreducibility, singular set unverified); point 7 that dim P = 0 for the PIII(D8) row, which bears on C3's single-fibre objection. Family membership of object A is NOT ESTABLISHED.", "label": "STRUCTURAL", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "CT-S13-COLDREAD5/compute_system_a.py", "output_hash": "8a9ec5c052f1c7c287857e873b63458e4c78d52f76535f60a6933e9c76f5fef4", "review": "cold", "review_note": "cold: CT-S13-COLDREAD5 worked from a self-contained packet with no access to CT-S4-FORMAL-TYPE, CT-S5B-COVER, CLASSIFICATION-TABLE.md, any DRAFT-*, VERIFY-*, AUDIT.md or REPORT.md. It recomputed the Katz data in its own SymPy script (compute_system_a.py) and read Table 2.1 from the rendered page images, not an OCR layer. Different code and independent reading of the primary source."}
{"claim_id": "R1-56", "task_id": "CT-R1-AUDIT-R9", "claim": "CORRECTION to R1-55 under operator review #6. The dim P = 0 note in C4 point 7 conflated two distinct things. P is the PARAMETER space of the family (vdP-Saito p.2634: 'a space of parameters P ... consisting of traces or eigenvalues of the matrices'), so dim P = 0 means PIII(D8) has no free parameters. That is expected and is NOT a defect, and it says nothing about the isomonodromic TIME variable, which still gives a one-dimensional deformation. The link CT-S13 drew to C3's single-fibre concern is a conflation and has been removed: C3 concerns the absence of a WRITTEN deformation, not the absence of parameters. Whether object A lies in a deformation is recorded as a separate open question.", "label": "STRUCTURAL", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "append_r9_claims.py", "output_hash": "bc2f5e49d66a6906be6941ff072b7727a1672840b0ca5f26af3ecd72533533e8", "review": "cold", "review_note": "cold-read by CT-S15-COLDREAD-DEFERRED, verdict CORRECT WITH WORDING CHANGE; the wording refinement is adopted as R1-93 and the claim now rests on the direct textual support of R1-92 rather than on an inference."}
{"claim_id": "R1-57", "task_id": "CT-R1-AUDIT-R9", "claim": "Recorded as a POSSIBLE APPROACH ONLY, carrying no weight: the quadratic cover of object A lands in the (1,-,1) row, which is NOT one of the two types vdP-Saito exempt from the strong Riemann-Hilbert guarantee. Whether the pullback can be used to decide the strong Riemann-Hilbert condition for object A itself is UNVERIFIED; the relation between the two problems has not been examined.", "label": "CONJECTURED", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "append_r9_claims.py", "output_hash": "bc2f5e49d66a6906be6941ff072b7727a1672840b0ca5f26af3ecd72533533e8", "review": "self", "review_note": "self: authoring change to the draft notice made by this session under operator ruling; no independent party has read the revised wording."}
{"claim_id": "R1-58", "task_id": "CT-R1-AUDIT-R9", "claim": "C2 restructured under operator ruling to lead with the ground that depends on nothing proved in this work: the companion's own theta_1 = theta_2 = 0, the companion's own stated scaling law, and Jimbo's published dictionary, all verified from page images. gamma = 1 - theta_0 - theta_t = 1 contradicts the published gamma = 0 using published sources alone. The apparency ground via C1 now follows as explicitly labelled independent corroboration, with the note that C1 leaves the exponent values intact and changes only the monodromy.", "label": "STRUCTURAL", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "append_r9_claims.py", "output_hash": "bc2f5e49d66a6906be6941ff072b7727a1672840b0ca5f26af3ecd72533533e8", "review": "self", "review_note": "self: authoring change to the draft notice made by this session under operator ruling; no independent party has read the revised wording."}
{"claim_id": "R1-59", "task_id": "CT-R1-AUDIT-R9", "claim": "C5 rewritten under operator ruling so that the notice RECORDS what fails rather than rebuilding the argument: item 1 refuted citing C1; the 'complete explanation' characterisation withdrawn; items 2-4 stated to not depend on apparency, with the explicit scope statement that their correctness is NOT re-examined in this notice. The words 'survive', 'stand' and 'unaffected' are avoided as endorsements, since nothing in this work has independently checked items 2-4. The same scope statement is applied to the untouched conclusions of Sec 2.2.", "label": "STRUCTURAL", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "append_r9_claims.py", "output_hash": "bc2f5e49d66a6906be6941ff072b7727a1672840b0ca5f26af3ecd72533533e8", "review": "self", "review_note": "self: authoring change to the draft notice made by this session under operator ruling; no independent party has read the revised wording."}
