{"claim_id": "R1-82", "task_id": "R11-S14", "claim": "Object B's trace-free normal form, pulled back by z=1/x, is EXACTLY equal to the trace-free normal potential of companion v1.2's printed ODE: both equal (12x^4+4x^3+4x^2+11)/(4(3x^2+x+1)^2). Symbolic difference is identically zero. Objects B and C are therefore PROJECTIVELY EQUIVALENT under z -> 1/x: related by that change of variable together with a scalar (rank-1) gauge transformation. They are NOT the same operator - their printed forms differ by the twist A^(-1/2), which alters the trace. The phrase 'the same object' was too strong and has been withdrawn.", "label": "PROVEN", "evidence_type": "computation", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "verify_s14.py", "output_hash": "717f8dc9c6307ff8ec44227117a4170ccc67cac1ee253d06969617aaf59ca7f9", "review": "cold", "review_note": "CT-S14-COLDREAD-B derived this independently under isolation; re-derived here from the primary printed data in different code."}
{"claim_id": "R1-83", "task_id": "R11-S14", "claim": "Under z=1/x the pullback's first-order term 2/x contributes nothing to the normal potential, since (2/x)^2/4 + d/dx(2/x)/2 = 1/x^2 - 1/x^2 = 0. Hence inversion ALONE reaches object B's trace-free normal form; no twist is required for its Table 2.1 row.", "label": "PROVEN", "evidence_type": "computation", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "verify_s14.py", "output_hash": "717f8dc9c6307ff8ec44227117a4170ccc67cac1ee253d06969617aaf59ca7f9", "review": "cold", "review_note": "implicit in CT-S14 task 2; verified explicitly here."}
{"claim_id": "R1-84", "task_id": "R11-S14", "claim": "The inversion x=1/z carries object B's finite singular points (-1 +/- i*sqrt(11))/2 exactly onto the companion operator's (-1 +/- i*sqrt(11))/6, resolving the previously unexplained /2 vs /6 discrepancy between the two objects.", "label": "PROVEN", "evidence_type": "computation", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "verify_roots.out.txt", "output_hash": "8e5d18c77f4504ee3bb896437ec829eda5f15d3fdba3a5569f68548577b0aee3", "review": "cold", "review_note": "elementwise check; an earlier set comparison printed False as a SymPy hashing artefact on unevaluated radicals, recorded in VERIFY-S14.md."}
