{"claim_id": "R1-87", "task_id": "R12-WORDING", "claim": "WORDING CORRECTION under operator review #9: 'B and C are the same object' is too strong for a notice about loose identity claims. What was shown is identical trace-free normal forms under z -> 1/x, i.e. PROJECTIVE EQUIVALENCE (change of variable plus rank-1 gauge). The printed operators differ by a trace-altering twist, so they are not the same operator. Notice and claim text updated.", "label": "STRUCTURAL", "evidence_type": "proof", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "verify_s14.py", "output_hash": "717f8dc9c6307ff8ec44227117a4170ccc67cac1ee253d06969617aaf59ca7f9", "review": "self", "review_note": "operator-supplied correction, adopted; it tightens a label rather than changing a computation."}
{"claim_id": "R1-88", "task_id": "R12-WORDING", "claim": "The three object names form TWO equivalence classes, not three unrelated objects: object A (what Channel Theory computes on) and the class {B, C}. The conflation C4 corrects is precisely between A and the {B,C} class, which is the one the Dtilde5 label fits. This sharpens C4 rather than weakening it.", "label": "STRUCTURAL", "evidence_type": "proof", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": "verify_s14.py", "output_hash": "717f8dc9c6307ff8ec44227117a4170ccc67cac1ee253d06969617aaf59ca7f9", "review": "self", "review_note": "follows from R1-82 (cold) plus the distinctness of A's Katz type."}
{"claim_id": "R1-89", "task_id": "R12-OPENQ", "claim": "RECORDED AS FUTURE PROBLEM, NOT A RESULT: because B and C are projectively equivalent under z -> 1/x, the isomonodromic embedding question need be posed only once; a deformation built for either, transported by the equivalence, settles the other. This reduces two open questions to one but does not make the remaining one easier, since a deformation must still be written down. Anyone attempting the transport must check that z -> 1/x carries C's time t = -+2i*sqrt(33)/9 to a consistent time for B. That check has NOT been performed.", "label": "CONJECTURED", "evidence_type": "proof", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": null, "output_hash": null, "review": "self", "review_note": "recorded as an open problem; no weight rests on it."}
