{"claim_id": "R1-92", "task_id": "R13-S15", "claim": "van der Put-Saito p.2635, immediately after Table 2.1, reads verbatim: 'We will also describe the corresponding one-dimensional families of differential modules M(t).' Read directly from the page image vdps_p2635.png. This is DIRECT textual evidence that dim P = 0 does not negate a one-dimensional deformation direction, replacing the inference R1-56 previously rested on.", "label": "INSPECTED", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": null, "output_hash": "56194f2639b0aa20d6e96863373e92ee599165e357b6b4b8c9221474b070da6b", "review": "cold", "review_note": "located by CT-S15-COLDREAD-DEFERRED under isolation; re-read here directly from the page image, not from OCR."}
{"claim_id": "R1-93", "task_id": "R13-S15", "claim": "WORDING REFINEMENT to R1-56, adopted from CT-S15: P should not be called simply 'the parameter space of the family'. Per p.2634 it is 'a space of parameters P (related to the parameters spaces of the Painleve equations) consisting of traces or eigenvalues of the matrices involved in the construction of R', and per p.2635 'R -> P is a family of affine cubic surfaces'. P is the base of a cubic-surface fibration on the MONODROMY side.", "label": "INSPECTED", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": null, "output_hash": "84b9dfc95b00d64c28ecb80a9477e64f07b44164b7db45bad8de819cb61ab9d0", "review": "cold", "review_note": "both quotes re-read directly from the page images."}
{"claim_id": "R1-94", "task_id": "R13-S15", "claim": "Table 2.1's r(t) column is a KATZ-INVARIANT column for a singular point named t, present only when the singular set contains one: the PVI row (0,0,0,0) has r(t)=0 with S={0,1,inf,t}, whereas the PIII(D8) row has r(t)='-'. The letter t does two different jobs on p.2635, which is the confusion R1-56 exists to prevent.", "label": "INSPECTED", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": null, "output_hash": "56194f2639b0aa20d6e96863373e92ee599165e357b6b4b8c9221474b070da6b", "review": "cold", "review_note": "read directly from the page image."}
{"claim_id": "R1-95", "task_id": "R13-S15", "claim": "REJECTED TRANSCRIPTION from CT-S15: it rendered the constant matrix in Jimbo's (3.1) as '(1/2) sigma_3' = diag(1/2,-1/2). The printed page carries diag(1,0). These differ by the trace shift (1/2)I and are different matrices. Caused by OCR. Not adopted; the notice does not quote (3.1), so it did not propagate.", "label": "INSPECTED", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": null, "output_hash": "84f548ceadd8d4a0e2d2f618b0bc384190bdfd9331c1138dd004ba9faa2cd2b5", "review": "self", "review_note": "rejection based on direct reading of jimbo_p1152.png."}
{"claim_id": "R1-96", "task_id": "R13-S15", "claim": "REJECTED TRANSCRIPTION from CT-S15: it reported (A1)_PV as non-integrality of theta_infinity, theta_0 and theta_t. The printed line is exactly 'theta_0, theta_t not in Z'; theta_infinity does NOT appear. This is a LOAD-BEARING hypothesis for C2. Caused by OCR. Not adopted. The notice's own line 116 states it correctly and was verified earlier by direct reading, so it did not propagate.", "label": "INSPECTED", "evidence_type": "file_inspection", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": null, "output_hash": "84f548ceadd8d4a0e2d2f618b0bc384190bdfd9331c1138dd004ba9faa2cd2b5", "review": "self", "review_note": "rejection based on direct reading of jimbo_p1152.png."}
{"claim_id": "R1-97", "task_id": "R13-METHOD", "claim": "P0 AMENDMENT: a load-bearing statement is read by LOOKING at the rendered page. Machine transcription of a page image, OCR included, is a text layer and does not satisfy the citation rule. An agent that cannot view an image must HALT and report that rather than OCR the page and proceed. Evidence: CT-S15 was given page images, ran OCR, and produced two transcription errors, one of them on a load-bearing hypothesis - the Gautschi (2.8) near-miss repeating one review after that lesson was recorded.", "label": "STRUCTURAL", "evidence_type": "proof", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": null, "output_hash": "7c16095744a9ab953d5255ec31172212979dfbcdc1558ccfa9f53c5831fabeda", "review": "self", "review_note": "method finding; reasoning in VERIFY-S15.md and P0-CITATION-RULE.md."}
{"claim_id": "R1-98", "task_id": "R13-S15", "claim": "Statement 2 verdict ADOPTED (CT-S15: CORRECT). To be an instance of Jimbo (3.1) an object must supply A_0(t) and A_t(t) as explicit t-dependent matrices, the singular points x=0 and x=t, eigenvalue data +/- theta_nu/2, and crucially the SECOND equation dY/dt = -A_t(t)/(x-t) Y. Scalar local data - singular points, exponents, formal type - supply none of these. The reasoning is independent of the two rejected transcriptions.", "label": "STRUCTURAL", "evidence_type": "proof", "dps": null, "reproducible": true, "script": null, "output_hash": "7c16095744a9ab953d5255ec31172212979dfbcdc1558ccfa9f53c5831fabeda", "review": "cold", "review_note": "CT-S15 reached this under isolation; the argument does not depend on its two OCR defects."}
